$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedures for Synthesis of 22 and 23. (i) A solution of
2-amino-5-bromopyrimidine (21) (1.6 g, 9.2 mmol) in DMSO (12 mL) and Et3N
(6 mL) was deoxygenated with a stream of N2. Addition of 1-pentyne (0.70
g, 1.0 mL, 10.25 mmol) was followed by (Ph3P)4Pd (530 mg, 0.46 mmol) and
CuI (140 mg, 0.74 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 5 h at 55 °C, and
volatiles were evaporated. The residue was suspended in hot MeOH and
filtered. Recrystallization (MeOH) gave
2-amino-5-(pent-1-yn-1-yl)pyrimidine (1.67 g, 79%). 1H NMR δ 1.04 (t, J =
7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.58-1.66 (m, 2H), 2.38 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 5.20 (br s,
2H), 8.32 (s, 2H); 13C NMR δ 13.5, 21.4, 22.1, 74.6, 93.5, 109.9, 160.4,
160.9; FAB-MS m/z 162 ([M + H+], 100%); HRMS m/z 162.1025 (M + H+
[C9H12N3] = 162.1031).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Antiviral Evaluation of
6-(Alkyl-heteroaryl)furo[2,3-d]pyrimidin-2(3H)-one Nucleosides and
Analogues with Ethynyl, Ethenyl, and Ethyl Spacers at C6 of the
Furopyrimidine Core
