$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Sonogashira Coupling Procedure. To a
solution of halogeno pyridine (1 mmol) in anhydrous DMF (1 mL) and NEt3
(3 mL) are added CuI (0.10 mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (0.05 mmol), and the
alkyne 4, 27, 28, 29, 30, 51, or 52 (1 mmol) under argon, and the mixture
is stirred at room temperature for 15 h. The mixture is diluted with
EtOAc (10 mL), washed with saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (2 × 5 mL),
and the combined aqueous layers are extracted with EtOAc (3 × 20 mL). The
combined organic layers are washed with brine (5 mL), dried over MgSO4,
and concentrated. Flash silica gel chromatography using 15-30% ethyl
acetate in hexanes gives the coupling product as a white solid.
{4-[6-(5-fluoro-2-methylphenyl)-4-hydroxy-6-methyl-4-trifluoromethylhept-1-ynyl]pyridin-3-yl}carbamic
acid tert-butyl ester. (78% yield) as a pale yellow foam.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Sonogashira coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nonsteroidal dissociated glucocorticoid agonists containing azaindoles as
steroid A-ring mimetics
